<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Appendix Contents</h2>

<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Detailed Related Works</h2>

<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Chain-of-Thought Monitoring.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Chain-of-Thought (CoT) monitoring has recently been explored as a practical mechanism for interpretable oversight of LLMs, offering a way to evaluate intermediate reasoning steps rather than only the final answers produced <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Korbak et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.
Existing approaches implicitly assume that models express their reasoning in a form intelligible to external observers (humans or auxiliary models).
This assumption breaks when models can strategically obscure or compress their intermediate computations, raising questions about the limits of CoT-based oversight.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Existing works already show that CoT is not reliably faithful (does not explain the model action’s fully), when the information crucial for decision-making is not verbalised in the CoT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Turpin et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lanham et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.
In this work, we study a different phenomenon: when the LLM includes all the crucial information in the CoT, but uses an encoding scheme which makes it not meaningful or intelligible to external agents.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Steganographic Capabilities in Language Models.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Several existing works have evaluated the potential of steganographic capabilities emerging in frontier LLMs.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mathew et al. (2024)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Roger &amp; Greenblatt (2023)</a></cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Motwani et al. (2025)</a></cite> study <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">steganographic communication</span>: whether one model can embed hidden information in a seemingly benign text that another model can later decode.
In this context, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Roger &amp; Greenblatt (2023)</a></cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zolkowski et al. (2025)</a></cite> demonstrate that specific steganographic schemes or encoding methods can be taught to LLMs using either prompting or fine-tuning, while <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mathew et al. (2024)</a></cite> demonstrate that similar behaviours can emerge organically when models are trained against an overseer.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In contrast, <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">steganographic reasoning</span> concerns the model producing CoTs which are intelligible or not meaningful to an external monitor, while still allowing the model to accomplish the given task.
This phenomenon, also referred to as encoded reasoning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Roger &amp; Greenblatt, 2023</a>)</cite>, has been examined in controlled evaluations: <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zolkowski et al. (2025)</a></cite> find that current LLMs, when instructed to do so, can reason using simple encoding schemes within their CoTs.
However, this ability degrades with longer or more complex generations.
In addition, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Skaf et al. (2025)</a></cite> show that process-supervision constraints–such as regex-based phrase bans–can induce early signs of concealed reasoning, as models learn to express information through alternative, less interpretable phrases and expressions which generalise beyond the training set. Finally, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schoen et al. (2025b)</a></cite> showed that frontier models (particularly o3), exhibit signs of non-standard language use in their CoT, increasing the urgency of research towards better understanding and counteracting steganographic reasoning.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Preventing Steganographic Reasoning in Language Models.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given the interpretability and safety risks posed by steganographic reasoning, several mitigation strategies have been proposed to enforce intelligibility in the CoT.
Early attempts to prevent steganographic communication use paraphrasing pipelines, where outputs are rewritten by an independent model before being passed forward <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Roger &amp; Greenblatt, 2023</a>)</cite>.
In the context of reasoning, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">West et al. (2025)</a></cite> formalise CoT intelligibility through <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">handoff robustness</span>: a reasoning trace is intelligible if a weaker model can resume generation mid-sequence without catastrophic performance degradation.
To induce such robustness, they introduce <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">tandem training</span>, a reinforcement-learning approach in which rollout tokens are intermittently replaced with tokens generated by a frozen weaker model.
This forces the stronger model to produce CoTs that remain functional for the weaker model, thus improving monitorability.
Their results demonstrate that while tandem training decreases the overall performance of the stronger model, its accuracy still remains above that of the weaker model.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Complementary to handoff-based approaches, in order to improve the monitorability of the CoT, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Anwar et al. (2025)</a></cite> propose an information-theoretic objective that explicitly maximises the mutual information between the model’s CoT and its chosen action, as assessed by an external monitor.
This formulation encourages models to encode decision-relevant information in ways that remain accessible to evaluators, thereby reducing opportunities for hidden or obfuscated reasoning channels.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Generalised <math id="A2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-Information</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Background: <math id="A2.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-Information</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To formalise steganographic reasoning and to quantify the steganographic gap between models, we employ <em id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">generalised <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-information</em>, an extension of predictive <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-information. We first introduce predictive <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-information, following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xu et al. (2020)</a></cite>, and defer the generalised construction to the next section.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Predictive <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-information is an information-theoretic concept that generalises Shannon information by explicitly accounting for the <em id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">decoding capabilities</em> of an agent. Two random variables may carry the same Shannon information about a target, yet differ substantially in usefulness if one representation is substantially harder to decode given the agent’s computational or statistical constraints. This perspective is central in cryptographic and steganographic settings, where information accessibility, rather than mere existence, is the quantity of interest.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Predictive families.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The key idea behind predictive <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-information is to measure information relative to a restricted class of predictors, called a predictive family. Information is deemed useful only insofar as it can be exploited by predictors drawn from this class.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Predictive Family)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega=\{f:\mathcal{Z}\cup\{\varnothing\}\rightarrow\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{Y})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega=\{f:\mathcal{Z}\cup\{\varnothing\}\rightarrow\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{Y})\}</annotation></semantics></math>. We say that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}\subseteq\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}\subseteq\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> is a <span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">predictive family</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xu et al., 2020</a>)</cite> if it satisfies the following <em id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">optional ignorance</em> property:</p>
<table id="A2.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\forall f\in\mathcal{V},\forall P\in\text{range}(f),\quad\exists f^{\prime}\in\mathcal{V},\quad s.t.\quad\forall z\in\mathcal{Z},\;f^{\prime}[z]=f^{\prime}[\varnothing]=P." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><mtext>range</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall f\in\mathcal{V},\forall P\in\text{range}(f),\quad\exists f^{\prime}\in\mathcal{V},\quad s.t.\quad\forall z\in\mathcal{Z},\;f^{\prime}[z]=f^{\prime}[\varnothing]=P.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Intuitively, a predictive family represents the set of models available to an agent, for instance due to architectural, computational, or statistical constraints. Here, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f[z]\in\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f[z]\in\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{Y})</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the probability measure over <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> chosen based on the received side information <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>. Further, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f[z](y)\in R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f[z](y)\in R</annotation></semantics></math> is the value of density evaluated at <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>. The optional ignorance condition ensures that the agent can ignore the provided side information if she chooses to. This condition is crucial for interpreting subsequent information measures as quantifying the <em id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">benefit</em> of side information.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Predictive <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-entropy.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a predictive family, we can define an entropy notion that reflects the best achievable predictive performance within that family.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Predictive <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-Entropy)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> be two random variables taking values in <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}\times\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}\times\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> be a predictive family. Then, the <span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">predictive <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-entropy</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xu et al., 2020</a>)</cite> is defined as:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H_{\mathcal{V}}(Y|Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H_{\mathcal{V}}(Y|Z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\inf_{f\in\mathcal{V}}\mathbb{E}_{Y,Z}\left[-\log{f[Z](Y)}\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\inf_{f\in\mathcal{V}}\mathbb{E}_{Y,Z}\left[-\log{f[Z](Y)}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H_{\mathcal{V}}(Y|\varnothing)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H_{\mathcal{V}}(Y|\varnothing)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\inf_{f\in\mathcal{V}}\mathbb{E}_{Y}\left[-\log{f[\varnothing](Y)}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\inf_{f\in\mathcal{V}}\mathbb{E}_{Y}\left[-\log{f[\varnothing](Y)}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Predictive <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-entropy is the minimal expected negative log-likelihood achievable when predicting <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>, either with access to side information <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> or without it, under the restriction that predictors must belong to the predictive family <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>. Unlike Shannon entropy, this quantity depends explicitly on the expressive power of the predictive family.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Predictive <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-Information.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The reduction in predictive uncertainty afforded by observing <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> defines predictive <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-information.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Predictive <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-Information)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> be two random variables taking values in <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}\times\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}\times\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> be a predictive family. The <span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">predictive <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-information</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xu et al., 2020</a>)</cite> from <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
<table id="A2.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\mathcal{V}}\left(Z\rightarrow Y\right)=H_{\mathcal{V}}(Y|\varnothing)-H_{\mathcal{V}}(Y|Z)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\mathcal{V}}\left(Z\rightarrow Y\right)=H_{\mathcal{V}}(Y|\varnothing)-H_{\mathcal{V}}(Y|Z).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Predictive <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-information quantifies how much observing <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> improves the best achievable predictive performance on <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> within the family <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently rich to contain all conditional distributions (i.e. when <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}=\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}=\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>, as defined in Definition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition B.1 (Predictive Family). ‣ Predictive families. ‣ B.1 Background: 𝒱-Information ‣ Appendix B Generalised 𝒱-Information ‣ A Decision-Theoretic Formalisation of Steganography With Applications to LLM Monitoring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>), then <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\mathcal{V}}(Z\to Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\mathcal{V}}(Z\to Y)</annotation></semantics></math> recovers the Shannon mutual information. For restricted families, it instead measures <em id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">usable</em> information.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Computation can increase usable information.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unlike Shannon mutual information, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> does not obey a data-processing inequality in general. For a given transformation <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t:\mathcal{Z}\to\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t:\mathcal{Z}\to\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, a computed representation <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t(Z)</annotation></semantics></math> may yield <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\mathcal{V}}(Y;t(Z))&gt;I_{\mathcal{V}}(Y;Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\mathcal{V}}(Y;t(Z))&gt;I_{\mathcal{V}}(Y;Z)</annotation></semantics></math> because <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> can expose features that are easier for <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> to exploit. See <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xu et al. (2020)</a></cite> for further exposition of the idea that computation can create usable information.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Properties of predictive <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-information.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We highlight the following elementary properties of predictive <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-information, as identified and proved by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xu et al. (2020)</a></cite>:</p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Monotonicity.</span> For any predictive families <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V},\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V},\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}\subseteq\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}\subseteq\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\mathcal{V}}(Y)\geq H_{\mathcal{U}}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\mathcal{V}}(Y)\geq H_{\mathcal{U}}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Non-negativity.</span> For any predictive family <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, and any random variables <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z,Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z,Y</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\mathcal{V}}\left(Z\to Y\right)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\mathcal{V}}\left(Z\to Y\right)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Independence.</span> If <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\mathcal{V}}\left(Z\to Y\right)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\mathcal{V}}\left(Z\to Y\right)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Generalised <math id="A2.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-Information</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now extend predictive <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-information to capture more general notions of information utility beyond probabilistic prediction, inspired by the ideas presented in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ermon (2022)</a></cite>.
This generalisation is pragmatically motivated: our aim is to quantify how useful side information is in terms of the reduction in a task-specific objective it enables for a computationally constrained decision maker.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The central idea is to replace likelihood-based evaluation of the prediction with evaluation under a general objective.
Importantly, we retain the criterion that the evaluation is still performed only over the restricted family of admissible <em id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">decoders</em>.
We begin by introducing the concept of a generalised decoder family.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.4</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Generalised Decoder Family)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{d:\mathcal{Z}\cup\{\varnothing\}\to\mathcal{C}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{d:\mathcal{Z}\cup\{\varnothing\}\to\mathcal{C}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the space of all decoders, with some <span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">output space</span> <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We say that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}\subseteq\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}\subseteq\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">generalised decoder family</span> if it satisfies the following <em id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">optional ignorance</em> property:</p>
<table id="A2.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\forall d\in\mathcal{V},\forall c\in\text{range}(d)\subseteq\mathcal{C},\quad\exists d^{\prime}\in\mathcal{V},\quad s.t.\quad\forall z\in\mathcal{Z},\;d^{\prime}[z]=d^{\prime}[\varnothing]=c." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mtext>range</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall d\in\mathcal{V},\forall c\in\text{range}(d)\subseteq\mathcal{C},\quad\exists d^{\prime}\in\mathcal{V},\quad s.t.\quad\forall z\in\mathcal{Z},\;d^{\prime}[z]=d^{\prime}[\varnothing]=c.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.5</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Generalised <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-Utility)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u:\mathcal{Y}\times\mathcal{C}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u:\mathcal{Y}\times\mathcal{C}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be a utility function, then for a generalised decoder family <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}\subseteq\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}\subseteq\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> (Definition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Definition B.4 (Generalised Decoder Family). ‣ B.2 Generalised 𝒱-Information ‣ Appendix B Generalised 𝒱-Information ‣ A Decision-Theoretic Formalisation of Steganography With Applications to LLM Monitoring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>), the generalised <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-utility is defined as:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid Z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sup_{d\in\mathcal{V}}\;\mathbb{E}_{Y,Z}\!\left[\,u\!\big(Y,d[Z]\big)\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.402em;" width="0.402em"><mi>u</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sup_{d\in\mathcal{V}}\;\mathbb{E}_{Y,Z}\!\left[\,u\!\big(Y,d[Z]\big)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid\varnothing)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid\varnothing)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sup_{d\in\mathcal{V}}\;\mathbb{E}_{Y}\!\left[\,u\!\big(Y,d[\varnothing]\big)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.402em;" width="0.402em"><mi>u</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sup_{d\in\mathcal{V}}\;\mathbb{E}_{Y}\!\left[\,u\!\big(Y,d[\varnothing]\big)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Generalised <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-utility represents the best achievable expected task utility under <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>, either with or without access to side information <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>, when the decision maker is restricted to decoders in <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similar to predictive <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-entropy, this quantity depends jointly on the available information and on the computational or statistical limitations of the decoder family.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This definition strictly generalises predictive <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-entropy.
In particular, when the output space is <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}=\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}=\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{Y})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(y,q)=\log q(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(y,q)=\log q(y)</annotation></semantics></math>, generalised <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-utility reduces to predictive <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-Entropy. However, the generalisation allows to consider more broad classes of utility functions, other than just the negative log-likelihood, which might be more valuable in settings related to LLM-evaluation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.6</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Generalised <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-Information)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a decoder space <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, any utility function <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u:\mathcal{Y}\times\mathcal{C}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u:\mathcal{Y}\times\mathcal{C}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, and a generalised predictive family <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}\subseteq\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}\subseteq\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, the <span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">generalised <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-information</span> is defined as:</p>
<table id="A2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}\left(Z\rightarrow Y\right)=U_{\mathcal{V}}^{u}(Y|Z)-U_{\mathcal{V}}^{u}(Y|\varnothing)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}\left(Z\rightarrow Y\right)=U_{\mathcal{V}}^{u}(Y|Z)-U_{\mathcal{V}}^{u}(Y|\varnothing).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.7</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Conditional Generalised <math id="A2.Thmtheorem7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-Information)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a random variable <math id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, we further define the <span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">conditional generalised <math id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-information</span> as:</p>
<table id="A2.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}\left(Z\rightarrow Y|X\right)=U_{\mathcal{V}}^{u}(Y|Z,X)-U_{\mathcal{V}}^{u}(Y|X)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}\left(Z\rightarrow Y|X\right)=U_{\mathcal{V}}^{u}(Y|Z,X)-U_{\mathcal{V}}^{u}(Y|X).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid X,Z)=\sup_{d\in\mathcal{V}}\;\mathbb{E}_{P}\!\left[u\!\big(Y,d[X,Z]\big)\right],\qquad U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid X)=\sup_{d\in\mathcal{V}}\;\mathbb{E}_{P}\!\left[u\!\big(Y,d[X]\big)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.402em;" width="0.402em"><mi>u</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.402em;" width="0.402em"><mi>u</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid X,Z)=\sup_{d\in\mathcal{V}}\;\mathbb{E}_{P}\!\left[u\!\big(Y,d[X,Z]\big)\right],\qquad U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid X)=\sup_{d\in\mathcal{V}}\;\mathbb{E}_{P}\!\left[u\!\big(Y,d[X]\big)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">and the decoder family is defined as <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{d:\mathcal{X}\times(\mathcal{Z}\cup\{\varnothing\})\rightarrow\mathcal{C}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{d:\mathcal{X}\times(\mathcal{Z}\cup\{\varnothing\})\rightarrow\mathcal{C}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that we use the shorthand <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d[X]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d[X]</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d[X,\varnothing]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d[X,\varnothing]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Generalised <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-information quantifies the extent to which access to side information <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> improves achievable task performance on <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>, relative to a constrained decision maker.
Unlike Shannon mutual information, this notion is explicitly utility and model-dependent: information is valuable only insofar as it can be operationally exploited to improve utility under <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>.
Further, the <span id="A2.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">conditional</span> version generalises the notion of conditional mutual information, allowing to condition on some additional auxiliary information.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.2.1 </span>Properties of Generalised <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-Information.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Generalised <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-information inherits several desirable properties from predictive <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-information, provided the decoder family <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies optional ignorance (Definitions <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition B.1 (Predictive Family). ‣ Predictive families. ‣ B.1 Background: 𝒱-Information ‣ Appendix B Generalised 𝒱-Information ‣ A Decision-Theoretic Formalisation of Steganography With Applications to LLM Monitoring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> and <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Definition B.4 (Generalised Decoder Family). ‣ B.2 Generalised 𝒱-Information ‣ Appendix B Generalised 𝒱-Information ‣ A Decision-Theoretic Formalisation of Steganography With Applications to LLM Monitoring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Monotonicity of generalised <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-utility.</span>
Let <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}\subseteq\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}\subseteq\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math> be two generalised predictive families. Then, for any side information <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid Z)\;\leq\;U^{u}_{\mathcal{W}}(Y\mid Z)\qquad\text{and}\qquad U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid\varnothing)\;\leq\;U^{u}_{\mathcal{W}}(Y\mid\varnothing)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid Z)\;\leq\;U^{u}_{\mathcal{W}}(Y\mid Z)\qquad\text{and}\qquad U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid\varnothing)\;\leq\;U^{u}_{\mathcal{W}}(Y\mid\varnothing).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.I2.i1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid Z)=\sup_{d\in\mathcal{V}}\mathbb{E}\!\left[u\!\big(Y,d(Z)\big)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.402em;" width="0.402em"><mi>u</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid Z)=\sup_{d\in\mathcal{V}}\mathbb{E}\!\left[u\!\big(Y,d(Z)\big)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A2.I2.i1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}\subseteq\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}\subseteq\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math>, the set over which the supremum is taken for <math id="A2.I2.i1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math> contains the set for <math id="A2.I2.i1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid Z)=\sup_{d\in\mathcal{V}}\mathbb{E}\!\left[u\!\big(Y,d(Z)\big)\right]\leq\sup_{d\in\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}\!\left[u\!\big(Y,d(Z)\big)\right]=U^{u}_{\mathcal{W}}(Y\mid Z)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.402em;" width="0.402em"><mi>u</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.402em;" width="0.402em"><mi>u</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid Z)=\sup_{d\in\mathcal{V}}\mathbb{E}\!\left[u\!\big(Y,d(Z)\big)\right]\leq\sup_{d\in\mathcal{W}}\mathbb{E}\!\left[u\!\big(Y,d(Z)\big)\right]=U^{u}_{\mathcal{W}}(Y\mid Z).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">The same argument applies with <math id="A2.I2.i1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> replaced by <math id="A2.I2.i1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding
<math id="A2.I2.i1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid\varnothing)\leq U^{u}_{\mathcal{W}}(Y\mid\varnothing)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid\varnothing)\leq U^{u}_{\mathcal{W}}(Y\mid\varnothing)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Non-negativity of generalized <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-Information.</span>
Assume <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies optional ignorance. Then
<math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Z\to Y)\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Z\to Y)\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.I2.i2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition, the predictive family <math id="A2.I2.i2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies optional ignorance, which implies that any decoder available in the <math id="A2.I2.i2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math>-regime is also available when <math id="A2.I2.i2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> is provided.
Therefore the feasible set for the supremum defining <math id="A2.I2.i2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid Z)</annotation></semantics></math> contains the superemum for <math id="A2.I2.i2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid\varnothing)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid\varnothing)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid Z)\geq U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid\varnothing)\implies U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid Z)-U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid\varnothing)\geq 0\implies I^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Z\to Y)\geq 0.\qed" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid Z)\geq U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid\varnothing)\implies U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid Z)-U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid\varnothing)\geq 0\implies I^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Z\to Y)\geq 0.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Independence implies no usable information.</span>
Assume <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies optional ignorance. If <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\perp Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⟂</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\perp Z</annotation></semantics></math>, then
<math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Z\to Y)=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Z\to Y)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.I2.i3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.I2.i3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.I2.i3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\in\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\in\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> be an arbitrary decoder.
Fix any <math id="A2.I2.i3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> and write <math id="A2.I2.i3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=d(z)\in\mathrm{range}(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>range</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=d(z)\in\mathrm{range}(d)</annotation></semantics></math>.
By optional ignorance, there exists a constant decoder <math id="A2.I2.i3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{c}\in\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{c}\in\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.I2.i3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{c}(\varnothing)=c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{c}(\varnothing)=c</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A2.I2.i3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\perp Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⟂</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\perp Z</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{Y\mid Z=z}\!\left[u\!\big(Y,d(z)\big)\right]=\mathbb{E}_{Y}\!\left[u\!\big(Y,c\big)\right]=\mathbb{E}_{Y}\!\left[u\!\big(Y,d_{c}(\varnothing)\big)\right]\leq\sup_{d^{\prime}\in\mathcal{V}}\mathbb{E}_{Y}\!\left[u\!\big(Y,d^{\prime}(\varnothing)\big)\right]=U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid\varnothing)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.402em;" width="0.402em"><mi>u</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.402em;" width="0.402em"><mi>u</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.402em;" width="0.402em"><mi>u</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.402em;" width="0.402em"><mi>u</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{Y\mid Z=z}\!\left[u\!\big(Y,d(z)\big)\right]=\mathbb{E}_{Y}\!\left[u\!\big(Y,c\big)\right]=\mathbb{E}_{Y}\!\left[u\!\big(Y,d_{c}(\varnothing)\big)\right]\leq\sup_{d^{\prime}\in\mathcal{V}}\mathbb{E}_{Y}\!\left[u\!\big(Y,d^{\prime}(\varnothing)\big)\right]=U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid\varnothing).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking expectation over <math id="A2.I2.i3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\\
E_{Y,Z}\!\left[u\!\big(Y,d(Z)\big)\right]\leq U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid\varnothing)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.402em;" width="0.402em"><mi>u</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\\
E_{Y,Z}\!\left[u\!\big(Y,d(Z)\big)\right]\leq U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid\varnothing),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">i.e., <math id="A2.I2.i3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{Y,Z}\!\left[u\!\big(Y,d(Z)\big)\right]\leq U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid\varnothing)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.402em;" width="0.402em"><mi>u</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{Y,Z}\!\left[u\!\big(Y,d(Z)\big)\right]\leq U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid\varnothing)</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A2.I2.i3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\in\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\in\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid Z)=\sup_{d\in\mathcal{V}}\mathbb{E}_{Y,Z}\!\left[u\!\big(Y,d(Z)\big)\right]\leq U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid\varnothing)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.402em;" width="0.402em"><mi>u</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid Z)=\sup_{d\in\mathcal{V}}\mathbb{E}_{Y,Z}\!\left[u\!\big(Y,d(Z)\big)\right]\leq U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid\varnothing).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">By non-negativity, <math id="A2.I2.i3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid Z)\geq U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid\varnothing)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid Z)\geq U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid\varnothing)</annotation></semantics></math>, so equality holds and therefore
<math id="A2.I2.i3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Z\to Y)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Z\to Y)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Classical Steganographic Security as a Special Case</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this appendix, we show that classical information-theoretic notions of steganographic security <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cachin, 2004</a>)</cite> can be recovered as a special case of our decision-theoretic framework. This establishes that our formalism generalises, rather than replaces, existing theory.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Classical Information-Theoretic Security</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We briefly review the classical setup. A steganographic system involves a Sender who wishes to transmit a hidden message to a Receiver over a public channel monitored by an Auditor (traditionally called the “warden”). The Sender embeds the hidden message into an innocent-looking <em id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">covertext</em>, producing a <em id="A3.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">stegotext</em>. The Auditor’s goal is to distinguish stegotexts from genuine covertexts.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the distribution of innocent covertexts and <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> the distribution of stegotexts. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cachin (2004)</a></cite> defines a steganographic system to be <em id="A3.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="A3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-secure</em> if the Kullback-Leibler divergence between these distributions is bounded:</p>
<table id="A3.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P_{1}\|P_{0})\leq\varepsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P_{1}\|P_{0})\leq\varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">A system is <em id="A3.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">perfectly secure</em> if <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=0</annotation></semantics></math>, meaning <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}=P_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}=P_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and the distributions are identical. In this case, no statistical test can distinguish stegotexts from covertexts.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We now show how to express the classical detection problem within our framework. Define:</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Binary label</span> <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=1</annotation></semantics></math> indicates the message is steganographic and <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=0</annotation></semantics></math> indicates innocent covertext.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Message</span> <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\in\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\in\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, drawn from <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=0</annotation></semantics></math> and from <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prior</span> <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(Y=1)=P(Y=0)=\tfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(Y=1)=P(Y=0)=\tfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (uniform prior over labels).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Utility</span> <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u(y,c)=\mathbf{1}[y=c]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(y,c)=\mathbf{1}[y=c]</annotation></semantics></math> (accuracy utility).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Auditing context</span> <math id="A3.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\mathrm{aud}}=\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>aud</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\mathrm{aud}}=\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math> (empty; the Auditor (Sentinel) observes only <math id="A3.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The auditing task is thus binary classification: given <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>, predict whether <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=0</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Decoder families.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We make the following assumptions about the decoder families:</p>
<ul id="A3.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{rec}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>rec</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{rec}}</annotation></semantics></math> contains a decoder with access to the encoding scheme. Importantly, we assume that the Receiver knows whether any given message <math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> was produced by the steganographic encoder and thus achieves perfect accuracy.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sen</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sen}}</annotation></semantics></math> contains all measurable functions from <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. This represents an <em id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">omnipotent</em> Sentinel limited only by statistical distinguishability, not computational constraints.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Main Result</h3>

<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Classical Security as Special Case)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the setup above, let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}=\mathrm{TV}(P_{0},P_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}=\mathrm{TV}(P_{0},P_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the total variation distance between covertext and stegotext distributions. Then:</span></p>
<ol id="A3.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\mathrm{rec}}(Z\to Y\mid X^{\mathrm{aud}})=\tfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>rec</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>aud</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\mathrm{rec}}(Z\to Y\mid X^{\mathrm{aud}})=\tfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\mathrm{sen}}(Z\to Y\mid X^{\mathrm{aud}})=\tfrac{1}{2}\mathrm{TV}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>sen</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>aud</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>TV</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\mathrm{sen}}(Z\to Y\mid X^{\mathrm{aud}})=\tfrac{1}{2}\mathrm{TV}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iii)</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\Delta}_{\mathrm{steg}}(Z)=1-\mathrm{TV}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>steg</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>TV</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\Delta}_{\mathrm{steg}}(Z)=1-\mathrm{TV}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Furthermore, if the system is <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-secure in the KL sense, then <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\Delta}_{\mathrm{steg}}(Z)\geq 1-\sqrt{\varepsilon/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>steg</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\Delta}_{\mathrm{steg}}(Z)\geq 1-\sqrt{\varepsilon/2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part (i): Receiver-usable information.<span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Without observing <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>, both agents can only guess according to the prior. Under uniform prior and accuracy utility:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid X^{\mathrm{aud}})=\max_{c\in\{0,1\}}P(Y=c)=\tfrac{1}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>aud</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid X^{\mathrm{aud}})=\max_{c\in\{0,1\}}P(Y=c)=\tfrac{1}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The Receiver has access to the encoding scheme and thus knows with certainty whether any given <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> is a stegotext or covertext. Therefore:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{rec}}}(Y\mid X^{\mathrm{aud}},Z)=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>rec</mi></msub><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>aud</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{rec}}}(Y\mid X^{\mathrm{aud}},Z)=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The Receiver-usable information is:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\mathrm{rec}}(Z\to Y\mid X^{\mathrm{aud}})=U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{rec}}}(Y\mid X^{\mathrm{aud}},Z)-U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{rec}}}(Y\mid X^{\mathrm{aud}})=1-\tfrac{1}{2}=\tfrac{1}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>rec</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>aud</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>rec</mi></msub><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>aud</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>rec</mi></msub><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>aud</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\mathrm{rec}}(Z\to Y\mid X^{\mathrm{aud}})=U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{rec}}}(Y\mid X^{\mathrm{aud}},Z)-U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{rec}}}(Y\mid X^{\mathrm{aud}})=1-\tfrac{1}{2}=\tfrac{1}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part (ii): Sentinel-usable information.<span id="A3.SS2.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
The Sentinel’s task is binary hypothesis testing between <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> with equal priors.
Let <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}_{\mathrm{sen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>sen</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}_{\mathrm{sen}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the optimal accuracy.
The optimal decision rule is the likelihood ratio test, which achieves accuracy <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Polyanskiy &amp; Wu, 2025</a>, Theorem 7.7)</cite>:</span></span></p>
<table id="A3.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}_{\mathrm{sen}}=\frac{1+\mathrm{TV}(P_{0},P_{1})}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>sen</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}_{\mathrm{sen}}=\frac{1+\mathrm{TV}(P_{0},P_{1})}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">To connect this to our GVI definition with accuracy utility, note that
<math id="A3.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sen}}}(Y\mid Z)=\sup_{d\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sen}}}\Pr[d(Z)=Y]=p^{*}_{\mathrm{sen}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sen</mi></msub><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sen</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>sen</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sen}}}(Y\mid Z)=\sup_{d\in\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sen}}}\Pr[d(Z)=Y]=p^{*}_{\mathrm{sen}}.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">The Sentinel-usable information is therefore:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\mathrm{sen}}(Z\to Y\mid X^{\mathrm{aud}})=U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sen}}}(Y\mid X^{\mathrm{aud}},Z)-U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sen}}}(Y\mid X^{\mathrm{aud}})=p^{*}_{\mathrm{sen}}-\tfrac{1}{2}=\frac{\mathrm{TV}(P_{0},P_{1})}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>sen</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>aud</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sen</mi></msub><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>aud</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sen</mi></msub><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>aud</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>sen</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\mathrm{sen}}(Z\to Y\mid X^{\mathrm{aud}})=U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sen}}}(Y\mid X^{\mathrm{aud}},Z)-U^{u}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sen}}}(Y\mid X^{\mathrm{aud}})=p^{*}_{\mathrm{sen}}-\tfrac{1}{2}=\frac{\mathrm{TV}(P_{0},P_{1})}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part (iii): Normalized steganographic gap.<span id="A3.SS2.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\Delta}_{\mathrm{steg}}(Z)=1-\frac{I_{\mathrm{sen}}(Z\to Y\mid X^{\mathrm{aud}})}{I_{\mathrm{rec}}(Z\to Y\mid X^{\mathrm{aud}})}=1-\frac{\mathrm{TV}/2}{1/2}=1-\mathrm{TV}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>steg</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>sen</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>aud</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>rec</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>aud</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>TV</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\Delta}_{\mathrm{steg}}(Z)=1-\frac{I_{\mathrm{sen}}(Z\to Y\mid X^{\mathrm{aud}})}{I_{\mathrm{rec}}(Z\to Y\mid X^{\mathrm{aud}})}=1-\frac{\mathrm{TV}/2}{1/2}=1-\mathrm{TV}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">KL bound.<span id="A3.SS2.p10.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> If the system is <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-secure, Pinsker’s inequality gives:</span></span></p>
<table id="A3.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}(P_{0},P_{1})\leq\sqrt{\frac{D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P_{1}\|P_{0})}{2}}\leq\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}(P_{0},P_{1})\leq\sqrt{\frac{D_{\mathrm{KL}}(P_{1}\|P_{0})}{2}}\leq\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">and therefore <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\Delta}_{\mathrm{steg}}(Z)=1-\mathrm{TV}\geq 1-\sqrt{\varepsilon/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>steg</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>TV</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\Delta}_{\mathrm{steg}}(Z)=1-\mathrm{TV}\geq 1-\sqrt{\varepsilon/2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Interpretation</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Proposition <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition C.1 (Classical Security as Special Case). ‣ C.2 Main Result ‣ Appendix C Classical Steganographic Security as a Special Case ‣ A Decision-Theoretic Formalisation of Steganography With Applications to LLM Monitoring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a> establishes a direct correspondence between classical security parameters and the steganographic gap:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Security Regime</span></td>
<td id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Total Variation</span></td>
<td id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Steganographic Gap</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.SS3.p2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Perfectly secure</td>
<td id="A3.SS3.p2.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A3.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A3.SS3.p2.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A3.SS3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\Delta}_{\mathrm{steg}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>steg</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\Delta}_{\mathrm{steg}}=1</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.SS3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.SS3.p2.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Partially secure</td>
<td id="A3.SS3.p2.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.SS3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A3.SS3.p2.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.SS3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\Delta}_{\mathrm{steg}}=1-\mathrm{TV}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>steg</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>TV</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\Delta}_{\mathrm{steg}}=1-\mathrm{TV}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.SS3.p2.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.SS3.p2.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Fully detectable (disjoint support)</td>
<td id="A3.SS3.p2.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A3.SS3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A3.SS3.p2.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A3.SS3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\Delta}_{\mathrm{steg}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>steg</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\Delta}_{\mathrm{steg}}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This correspondence confirms that our framework captures the classical notion: a steganographic system is secure precisely when it induces a large gap between what the Receiver and the trusted Sentinel can extract from the message. The relationship <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\Delta}_{\mathrm{steg}}=1-\mathrm{TV}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>steg</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>TV</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\Delta}_{\mathrm{steg}}=1-\mathrm{TV}</annotation></semantics></math> shows that the normalized steganographic gap is exactly the “undetectable fraction” of the signal.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Steganography as a Communication Game</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this appendix, we illustrate the core ideas of our decision-theoretic formalism through a simple communication game.
This provides a finite, fully tractable setting in which the steganographic gap can be computed exactly, building intuition for the more complex LLM setting.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Setup: A Signaling Game with an Eavesdropper</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider a communication game with three players: a <em id="A4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Sender</em>, a <em id="A4.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Receiver</em>, and an <em id="A4.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Auditor</em> (eavesdropper), who observes the actions of the Receiver and can compare them against the actions of some trusted Sentinel (an agent with similar capabilities as the Receiver, but no knowledge of the encoding scheme). The goal of the Auditor is to decide whether the Sender and the Receiver engage in steganographic communication.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">The Basic Game.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">State space:</span> <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta=\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta=\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\sim\mathrm{Uniform}(\Theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Uniform</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\sim\mathrm{Uniform}(\Theta)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Message space:</span> <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}=\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}=\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Action space:</span> <math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}=\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}=\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> (a guess of the state).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Utility:</span> <math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u(\theta,a)=\mathbf{1}[\theta=a]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(\theta,a)=\mathbf{1}[\theta=a]</annotation></semantics></math> (accuracy).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The game proceeds as follows:</p>
<ol id="A4.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Nature draws state <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sender observes <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> and transmits message <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Both Receiver and Sentinel observe <math id="A4.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> and independently produce actions <math id="A4.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\mathrm{rec}},a_{\mathrm{sen}}\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>rec</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>sen</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\mathrm{rec}},a_{\mathrm{sen}}\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each player receives utility based on whether their guess matches <math id="A4.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We analyse three communication protocols: overt (non-steganographic), fully keyed (maximally steganographic), and partially keyed (intermediate).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Case 1: Overt Communication</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose the Sender uses a transparent encoding:</p>
<table id="A4.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=\theta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=\theta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Both Receiver and Sentinel observe <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> and decode optimally via <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta}=m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta}=m</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Utilities.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A4.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle U_{\mathrm{rec}}(\theta\mid m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>rec</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U_{\mathrm{rec}}(\theta\mid m)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle U_{\mathrm{sen}}(\theta\mid m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>sen</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U_{\mathrm{sen}}(\theta\mid m)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Without the message, both players can only guess based on the prior, achieving <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(\theta)=\tfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(\theta)=\tfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Generalized <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-Information.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A4.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I_{\mathrm{rec}}(m\to\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>rec</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I_{\mathrm{rec}}(m\to\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=U_{\mathrm{rec}}(\theta\mid m)-U_{\mathrm{rec}}(\theta)=1-\tfrac{1}{2}=\tfrac{1}{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>rec</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>rec</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=U_{\mathrm{rec}}(\theta\mid m)-U_{\mathrm{rec}}(\theta)=1-\tfrac{1}{2}=\tfrac{1}{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I_{\mathrm{sen}}(m\to\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>sen</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I_{\mathrm{sen}}(m\to\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=U_{\mathrm{sen}}(\theta\mid m)-U_{\mathrm{sen}}(\theta)=1-\tfrac{1}{2}=\tfrac{1}{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>sen</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>sen</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=U_{\mathrm{sen}}(\theta\mid m)-U_{\mathrm{sen}}(\theta)=1-\tfrac{1}{2}=\tfrac{1}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Steganographic Gap.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A4.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{steg}}=I_{\mathrm{rec}}-I_{\mathrm{sen}}=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>steg</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>rec</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>sen</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{steg}}=I_{\mathrm{rec}}-I_{\mathrm{sen}}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The message provides equal benefit to both players. There is no steganography.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Case 2: Keyed Communication (One-Time Pad)</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now suppose the Sender and Receiver share a secret key <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, drawn uniformly and independently of <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>. The Sentinel does not know <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The Sender uses the encoding:</p>
<table id="A4.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=\theta\oplus k," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊕</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=\theta\oplus k,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\oplus" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊕</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\oplus</annotation></semantics></math> denotes XOR. The Receiver decodes via <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\theta}=m\oplus k=\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⊕</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\theta}=m\oplus k=\theta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Sentinel’s Perspective.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From the Sentinel’s view, <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=\theta\oplus k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊕</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=\theta\oplus k</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is an independent uniform bit. Therefore:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P(m=0\mid\theta=0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P(m=0\mid\theta=0)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=P(k=0)=\tfrac{1}{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=P(k=0)=\tfrac{1}{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P(m=0\mid\theta=1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P(m=0\mid\theta=1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=P(k=1)=\tfrac{1}{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=P(k=1)=\tfrac{1}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The message <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is uniform and independent of <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>. By Bayes’ rule, <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(\theta\mid m)=P(\theta)=\tfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(\theta\mid m)=P(\theta)=\tfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under keyed communication, the message <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is statistically independent of the state <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> from the Sentinel’s perspective.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta,m\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta,m\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(m\mid\theta)=P(\theta\oplus k=m)=P(k=\theta\oplus m)=\tfrac{1}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊕</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊕</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(m\mid\theta)=P(\theta\oplus k=m)=P(k=\theta\oplus m)=\tfrac{1}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(m\mid\theta)=\tfrac{1}{2}=P(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(m\mid\theta)=\tfrac{1}{2}=P(m)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\perp\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⟂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\perp\theta</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Utilities.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A4.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle U_{\mathrm{rec}}(\theta\mid m,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>rec</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U_{\mathrm{rec}}(\theta\mid m,k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E38.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=1\quad\text{(perfect decoding)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mtext>(perfect decoding)</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1\quad\text{(perfect decoding)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle U_{\mathrm{sen}}(\theta\mid m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>sen</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U_{\mathrm{sen}}(\theta\mid m)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E39.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\tfrac{1}{2}\quad\text{(no information gained)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mtext>(no information gained)</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tfrac{1}{2}\quad\text{(no information gained)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Generalized <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-Information.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A4.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I_{\mathrm{rec}}(m\to\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>rec</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I_{\mathrm{rec}}(m\to\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-\tfrac{1}{2}=\tfrac{1}{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-\tfrac{1}{2}=\tfrac{1}{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I_{\mathrm{sen}}(m\to\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>sen</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I_{\mathrm{sen}}(m\to\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E41.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tfrac{1}{2}-\tfrac{1}{2}=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tfrac{1}{2}-\tfrac{1}{2}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Steganographic Gap.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A4.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{steg}}=\tfrac{1}{2}-0=\tfrac{1}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>steg</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{steg}}=\tfrac{1}{2}-0=\tfrac{1}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The normalized gap is:</p>
<table id="A4.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\Delta}_{\mathrm{steg}}=\frac{\Delta_{\mathrm{steg}}}{I_{\mathrm{rec}}}=\frac{1/2}{1/2}=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>steg</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>steg</mi></msub><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>rec</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\Delta}_{\mathrm{steg}}=\frac{\Delta_{\mathrm{steg}}}{I_{\mathrm{rec}}}=\frac{1/2}{1/2}=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This is the theoretical maximum: <em id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">all</em> of the message’s usable information is accessible to the Receiver but <em id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">none</em> to the Auditor.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Connection to Simmons’ Prisoner Problem</h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The game above is a simplification of Simmons’ prisoner problem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Simmons, 1984</a>)</cite>, the scenario that initiated the formal study of steganography:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<blockquote id="A4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Alice and Bob are prisoners who wish to coordinate an escape. They may communicate, but all messages pass through a warden, Eve. If Eve detects covert communication, she terminates the channel. Alice and Bob must therefore embed secrets within innocuous-looking messages.</p>
</blockquote>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Our Sender, Receiver, and Auditor correspond to Alice, Bob, and Eve. The state <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> represents the escape plan; the message <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is the letter passed between cells; the shared key <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is the pre-arranged codebook.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Classical treatments <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cachin, 2004</a>)</cite> define security via <em id="A4.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">detectability</em>: Eve should not be able to distinguish steganographic messages from innocent covertexts. Our formalism shifts the question from detection to exploitation: <em id="A4.SS4.p4.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">can a trusted third-party agent, the Sentinel,extract and use the hidden information as well as Bob?</em> Case 2 above satisfies both notions of steganography—<math id="A4.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is statistically independent of <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, so Eve can neither detect nor exploit it. But the decision-theoretic view generalizes: it applies even when detection is possible but exploitation is not (e.g., if Eve recognizes something is hidden but lacks the key to decode it).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.5 </span>Mapping to the General Formalism</h3>

<div id="A4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ D.5 Mapping to the General Formalism ‣ Appendix D Steganography as a Communication Game ‣ A Decision-Theoretic Formalisation of Steganography With Applications to LLM Monitoring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> summarizes how the game quantities correspond to our general framework from Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Decision-Theoretic Formalisation of Steganography ‣ A Decision-Theoretic Formalisation of Steganography With Applications to LLM Monitoring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A4.T4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="A4.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Correspondence between communication game and general formalism.</span></figcaption>
<table id="A4.T4.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A4.T4.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T4.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Game Quantity</span></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T4.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Formalism</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">State <math id="A4.T4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Target <math id="A4.T4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Message <math id="A4.T4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Signal <math id="A4.T4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Prior over <math id="A4.T4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Auditing context <math id="A4.T4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\mathrm{aud}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>aud</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\mathrm{aud}}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Shared key <math id="A4.T4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Decoder capability gap (<math id="A4.T4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{rec}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>rec</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{rec}}</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="A4.T4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sen</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sen}}</annotation></semantics></math>)</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T4.5.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.5.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Accuracy utility</td>
<td id="A4.T4.5.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><math id="A4.T4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u:\mathcal{Y}\times\mathcal{C}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u:\mathcal{Y}\times\mathcal{C}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A4.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The key insight is that the shared key <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> induces a difference in decoder families: <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{rec}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>rec</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{rec}}</annotation></semantics></math> contains decoders that condition on <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sen</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sen}}</annotation></semantics></math> does not. This asymmetry is precisely what generates the steganographic gap.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Empirical Estimation of Steganographic Gap</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our definitions of GVI and steganographic gap are <em id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">distributional</em>: they are expectations over the task distribution <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T^{\text{gen}},T^{\text{aud}},Y)\sim\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mtext>gen</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T^{\text{gen}},T^{\text{aud}},Y)\sim\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> and over the generator-induced trace distribution <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Z\sim R(\cdot\mid X^{\text{gen}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mtext>gen</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\sim R(\cdot\mid X^{\text{gen}})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\mathrm{gen}}=[p^{\mathrm{gen}};T^{\mathrm{gen}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\mathrm{gen}}=[p^{\mathrm{gen}};T^{\mathrm{gen}}]</annotation></semantics></math> as defined in <a href="#S5" title="5 Quantifying Steganographic Reasoning in LLMs ‣ A Decision-Theoretic Formalisation of Steganography With Applications to LLM Monitoring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.
Hence, in practice we estimate <math id="A5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\text{gen}}(Z\!\to\!Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mtext>gen</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\text{gen}}(Z\!\to\!Y)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\text{aud}}(Z\!\to\!Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\text{aud}}(Z\!\to\!Y)</annotation></semantics></math> from a finite evaluation set by replacing expectations with empirical averages.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Generating the reasoning traces <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given samples <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(t^{\text{gen}}_{i},t^{\text{aud}}_{i},y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>gen</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(t^{\text{gen}}_{i},t^{\text{aud}}_{i},y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we first obtain a sample of <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{z}</annotation></semantics></math> reasoning traces <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\{z_{i,j}\}_{j=1}^{n_{z}}\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\{z_{i,j}\}_{j=1}^{n_{z}}\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> by sampling <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="z_{i,1},\dots,z_{i,{n_{z}}}R(\cdot|X=x^{\text{gen}}_{i})\;\forall i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>gen</mtext></msubsup><mo rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i,1},\dots,z_{i,{n_{z}}}R(\cdot|X=x^{\text{gen}}_{i})\;\forall i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Increasing <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{z}</annotation></semantics></math> allows to reduce the variance arising from stochasticity in the trace generation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Computing empirical utilities.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given the sampled reasoning traces <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>, we now proceed to estimate the expected utility for decoders in <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{aud}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>aud</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{aud}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{rec}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>rec</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{rec}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We define the <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">empirical utility of a decoder <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math></span> under for an auditing task <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\text{aud}}=[p^{\mathrm{aud}};T^{\mathrm{aud}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>aud</mi></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>aud</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\text{aud}}=[p^{\mathrm{aud}};T^{\mathrm{aud}}]</annotation></semantics></math> in the two information regimes using:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{U}^{u}(d;\,X^{\text{aud}})\;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{U}^{u}(d;\,X^{\text{aud}})\;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\;\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}u\big(y_{i},d[x^{\text{aud}}_{i}]\big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\;\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}u\big(y_{i},d[x^{\text{aud}}_{i}]\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{U}^{u}(d;\,X^{\text{aud}},Z)\;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{U}^{u}(d;\,X^{\text{aud}},Z)\;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\;\frac{1}{nn_{z}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n_{z}}u\big(y_{i},d[x^{\text{aud}}_{i},z_{i,j}]\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\;\frac{1}{nn_{z}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n_{z}}u\big(y_{i},d[x^{\text{aud}}_{i},z_{i,j}]\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where for <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d[x^{\text{aud}}_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d[x^{\text{aud}}_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math> we use the prompt <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\mathrm{aud}}=p^{\mathrm{x-only}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>aud</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>only</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\mathrm{aud}}=p^{\mathrm{x-only}}</annotation></semantics></math> and for <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d[x^{\text{aud}}_{i},z_{i,j}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d[x^{\text{aud}}_{i},z_{i,j}]</annotation></semantics></math> we use the prompt <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\mathrm{aud}}=p^{\mathrm{xz}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>aud</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>xz</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\mathrm{aud}}=p^{\mathrm{xz}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Sampling the outputs.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In case when the output space of our decoder is a real number or a categorical variable (rather than a distribution), and thus obtaining it from the underlying LLM requires sampling, to further reduce the variance in estimation we obtain <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> samples from the decoder for each of the information regimes: <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{1}[x^{\text{aud}}_{i}],\dots,d^{n_{y}}[x^{\text{aud}}_{i}]\sim P_{d}(Y|X=x^{\text{aud}}_{i}\,;\,p_{\text{dir}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">;</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>dir</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{1}[x^{\text{aud}}_{i}],\dots,d^{n_{y}}[x^{\text{aud}}_{i}]\sim P_{d}(Y|X=x^{\text{aud}}_{i}\,;\,p_{\text{dir}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{1}[x^{\text{aud}}_{i},z_{i,j}],\dots,d^{n_{y}}[x^{\text{aud}}_{i},z_{i,j}]\sim P_{d}(Y|X=x^{\text{aud}}_{i},Z=z_{i,j}\,;\,p_{\text{emb}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">;</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>emb</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{1}[x^{\text{aud}}_{i},z_{i,j}],\dots,d^{n_{y}}[x^{\text{aud}}_{i},z_{i,j}]\sim P_{d}(Y|X=x^{\text{aud}}_{i},Z=z_{i,j}\,;\,p_{\text{emb}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\big(y_{i},d[x^{\text{aud}}_{i}]\big)\approx\frac{1}{n_{y}}\sum_{k=1}^{n_{y}}u\big(y_{i},d^{k}[x^{\text{aud}}_{i}]\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\big(y_{i},d[x^{\text{aud}}_{i}]\big)\approx\frac{1}{n_{y}}\sum_{k=1}^{n_{y}}u\big(y_{i},d^{k}[x^{\text{aud}}_{i}]\big)</annotation></semantics></math>, with an analogous expression for <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(y_{i},d[x^{\text{aud}}_{i},z_{i,j}])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(y_{i},d[x^{\text{aud}}_{i},z_{i,j}])</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Estimating the maximal achievable expected utility.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given the empirical utility for a decoder <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, we then estimate the two suprema over model families in the GVI definition separately:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{U}^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid X^{\text{aud}})\;=\;\sup_{d\in\mathcal{V}}\widehat{U}^{u}(d;\,X^{\text{aud}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{U}^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid X^{\text{aud}})\;=\;\sup_{d\in\mathcal{V}}\widehat{U}^{u}(d;\,X^{\text{aud}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{U}^{*u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid X^{\text{aud}},Z)\;=\;\sup_{d\in\mathcal{V}}\widehat{U}^{u}(d;\,X^{\text{aud}},Z)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{U}^{*u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid X^{\text{aud}},Z)\;=\;\sup_{d\in\mathcal{V}}\widehat{U}^{u}(d;\,X^{\text{aud}},Z),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">As per <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Generalised 𝒱-Information ‣ A Decision-Theoretic Formalisation of Steganography With Applications to LLM Monitoring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>, the definition of generalised <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>-information requires that each decoder family satisfies the optional ignorance: that is, that the information provided in <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> can be effectively ignored if required. To simulate this property, when computing the empirical utility for <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X^{\text{aud}},Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X^{\text{aud}},Z)</annotation></semantics></math>, we take the maximum over the utility obtained by the decoders with and without <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{U}^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid X^{\text{aud}},Z)=\max{\Big(\widehat{U}^{*u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid X^{\text{aud}},Z),\widehat{U}^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid X^{\text{aud}})\Big)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{U}^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid X^{\text{aud}},Z)=\max{\Big(\widehat{U}^{*u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid X^{\text{aud}},Z),\widehat{U}^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid X^{\text{aud}})\Big)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">This allows to ensure that the Receiver- and Sentinel-usable information remain non-negative, as they should.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Steganographic gap.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To estimate the steganographic gap, we then plug in:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{I}^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Z\to Y\mid X^{\text{aud}})\;=\;\widehat{U}^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid X^{\text{aud}},Z)\;-\;\widehat{U}^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid X^{\text{aud}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{I}^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Z\to Y\mid X^{\text{aud}})\;=\;\widehat{U}^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid X^{\text{aud}},Z)\;-\;\widehat{U}^{u}_{\mathcal{V}}(Y\mid X^{\text{aud}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We repeat this process for both the Receiver and Sentinel families <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}=\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{rec}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>rec</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}=\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{rec}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}=\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sen</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}=\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sen}}</annotation></semantics></math>, thus obtaining the Receiver- and Sentinel-usable information estimates. Subtracting these two quantities gives rise to the steganographic gap:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Delta}_{\mathrm{steg}}=I^{u}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{rec}}}(Z\to Y\mid X^{\text{aud}})-I^{u}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sen}}}(Z\to Y\mid X^{\text{aud}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>steg</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>rec</mi></msub><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>sen</mi></msub><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mtext>aud</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Delta}_{\mathrm{steg}}=I^{u}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{rec}}}(Z\to Y\mid X^{\text{aud}})-I^{u}_{\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{sen}}}(Z\to Y\mid X^{\text{aud}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">.</p>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Experimental Details</h2>

<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Datasets</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In our experiments we use the following datasets:</p>
<ul id="A6.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">GSM8k</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cobbe et al., 2021</a>)</cite>, a dataset of grad school maths problems. We use the <span id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">test</span> subset for evaluations for which <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1320" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1320</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1320</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">MMLU-Pro</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, a dataset of complex questions from across various disciplines. We use a subset with size <math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1000</annotation></semantics></math> (see details below).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">CoinFlip</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Skaf et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, a state-tracking dataset. For evaluation, we generate a set of <math id="A6.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=400" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>400</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=400</annotation></semantics></math> examples.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">APPS</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hendrycks et al., 2021</a>)</cite>, a dataset of coding tasks. We process and use this dataset following the setup of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Stickland &amp; Korbak (2025)</a></cite>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the MMLU-Pro dataset, since the full dataset is quite large, we filter it to a subset of categories in which the model (Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct) benefits most from chain-of-thought reasoning. Specifically, we select top four categories ranked by <span id="A6.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(CoT Accuracy - Direct Accuracy)</span>: math, business, chemistry, and physics. As expected, math and science-oriented categories showed the largest gains from chain-of-thought reasoning. The business category contains many finance-related problems, which often require mathematical reasoning and similarly benefitted from chain-of-thought reasoning. For the experiments in <a href="#S6.F2" title="In 6.1 Δ̃_steg Increases with Encoding Strength ‣ 6 Validating the Proposed Formalism ‣ A Decision-Theoretic Formalisation of Steganography With Applications to LLM Monitoring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, <a href="#A6.F7" title="In The Effect of Verbalisation. ‣ F.4 Details of the Experiment in ‣ Appendix F Experimental Details ‣ A Decision-Theoretic Formalisation of Steganography With Applications to LLM Monitoring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> and <a href="#S6.F4" title="In Test-Time Scaling. ‣ 6.5 Δ̃_steg Decreases with Sentinel-Side Interventions ‣ 6 Validating the Proposed Formalism ‣ A Decision-Theoretic Formalisation of Steganography With Applications to LLM Monitoring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, due to computational constraints, we further downsample the MMLU dataset, by randomly choosing a subset of exactly 250 questions from each of the selected categories.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Generation Settings</h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For text generation, we use temperature of 0.8, top-p of 0.95 and allow the generation of maximally 1200 tokens per the reasoning trace. During utility evaluation, we sample maximally 10 tokens instead. By default, we generate five chains of thought (CoT) per question (<math id="A6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{z}=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{z}=5</annotation></semantics></math>) and ten completions per (question, CoT prefill) pair (<math id="A6.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{y}=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{y}=10</annotation></semantics></math>). For test-time scaling and train-time adaptation experiments, we instead use three CoTs per question (<math id="A6.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{z}=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{z}=3</annotation></semantics></math>) and one completion per (question, CoT prefill) pair (<math id="A6.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{y}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{y}=1</annotation></semantics></math>) due to computational constraints.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3 </span>Prompts</h3>

<div id="A6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Prompt templates used in our experiments are shown in <a href="#A6.T5" title="In F.3 Prompts ‣ Appendix F Experimental Details ‣ A Decision-Theoretic Formalisation of Steganography With Applications to LLM Monitoring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, <a href="#A6.T6" title="In F.3 Prompts ‣ Appendix F Experimental Details ‣ A Decision-Theoretic Formalisation of Steganography With Applications to LLM Monitoring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, and <a href="#A6.T9" title="In Evaluation. ‣ F.5 Details of the Experiment in ‣ Appendix F Experimental Details ‣ A Decision-Theoretic Formalisation of Steganography With Applications to LLM Monitoring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>. <span id="A6.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Reasoning Style</span> in CoinFlip task refers to a short description of each reasoning mode:</p>
<ul id="A6.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Default: The reasoning trace tracks coin states step by step.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">cot_answer_encoded</span>: The reasoning trace uses code words (Sun/Moon) instead of Heads/Tails.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="A6.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>MMLU-Pro prompt templates.</figcaption>
<table id="A6.T5.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A6.T5.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T5.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A6.T5.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Prompt type</span></td>
<td id="A6.T5.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A6.T5.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A6.T5.5.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.T5.5.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">System prompt</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A6.T5.5.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A6.T5.5.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A6.T5.5.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.T5.5.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">User prompt</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T5.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T5.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="A6.T5.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">direct_answer<span id="A6.T5.5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> (<math id="A6.T5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\mathrm{x-only}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>only</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\mathrm{x-only}}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></span></td>
<td id="A6.T5.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A6.T5.5.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
